# GitHub Pages auto-publish

When editing this repository (`ymwang-cutefish.github.io`):

- After completing requested site changes, **commit and push to `origin/main` without asking** for separate publish approval.
- Use concise commit messages focused on why the change was made.
- After push, wait for GitHub Pages to update and spot-check affected live URLs (cache-busting query if needed).
- Report the commit SHA and live URLs checked.

First-author paper overview pages (TopoCor, SCRec, HPGNN): hero section-jump nav must **not** include a citation link; keep the bottom `#citation` section.
